__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
data/
# dataset files stay ignored for size, but keep the tracked pointer/checksum
!benchmarks/data/
benchmarks/data/*
!benchmarks/data/README.md
# tiny pre-registered eval sets are tracked (not datasets)
!benchmarks/data/collections_eval_questions.json
*.rknn
*.rkllm
models/minilm-onnx/model.onnx
models/cross-encoder-onnx/
.env
*.log
eval/reports/
.superpowers/

# Secret material: PATTERN-based, not a per-file allowlist.
# A per-file list cannot stop a NEW file, which is exactly how a fresh
# data/hub/identity.json with plaintext signing_private and encryption_private
# walked into jaylfc/taOS PR #2043 (commit 42422c3b). It was removed before
# merge, but the blob stays reachable from refs/pull/2043/head, so treat it as
# public. Verified before adding: zero currently-tracked files match these
# patterns, so nothing working was un-tracked. Keep them NARROW for that reason
# (a broad *credential* glob would silently eat source and test files).
*.key
*.pem
*.p8
*_private*
*private_key*
identity.json
*credentials.json
creds*.json
.env.*
id_rsa
id_ed25519
